{
  "slug": "precommit-registry",
  "title": "Precommit registry: one name, one owner-signed opening",
  "kind": "coin_puzzle",
  "security_scope": "Original WIP teaching policy, not ready for real funds. A one-slot registry coin curries the exact precommit module hash. Its solution opens a commitment (owner key, receipt destination, salt) for the fixed name. It recomputes the commitment and the genuine precommit coin ID from the parent, curried puzzle hash and price, asserts that coin's ready announcement, announces acceptance, requires the owner's AGG_SIG_ME and creates a one-mojo owner receipt. Spending the slot once consumes it.",
  "environment": "strict",
  "reference_mode": "module",
  "provenance": {
    "classification": "original teaching implementation",
    "references": [
      "https://chialisp.com/conditions/",
      "https://chialisp.com/chialisp-currying/",
      "https://github.com/judeallred/chialisp-oxide/issues/17"
    ],
    "source_origin": "All six paired source files are original implementations of this explicit teaching contract. No XCHandles, CATalog or other published module is copied, ported or claimed.",
    "limitations": [
      "One fixed name and one registry slot coin; not a dynamic namespace, renewable name service or transfer protocol.",
      "A mature precommit stays claimable until someone refunds it; there is no upper claim age. Speculative mature precommits for guessable names can still compete, and nothing establishes first-committer-wins or censorship resistance.",
      "The salt must be unpredictable; the chain checks its length, not its entropy. Fixture salts are public test data.",
      "SHA-256 collision and preimage resistance are assumptions. Proof models do not cover SHA, these exports or the two-coin protocol."
    ]
  },
  "source_dependencies": [
    "crates/chialisp-oxide/src/lib.rs",
